931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-104343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}}=[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{-5}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =3\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}} & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{-5} \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(-5)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(-5)\\theta )] \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )]=6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-104343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2392448160f40f4b2950be85e254ffe26679a0f9efd98c33f481c3aa954de7e"} {"question" "q-104343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/hom