{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta )]=2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-104122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2392448160f40f4b2950be85e254ffe26679a0f9efd98c33f481c3aa954de7e"} {"question" "q-104122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-104122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]"] ["math" "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )]"] ["math" "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-104122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{5}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{5}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-5}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\theta )\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2392448160f40f4b2950be85e254ffe26679a0f9efd98c33f481c3aa954de7e"} {"question" "q-325342" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325342" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(5\\theta)+i\\sin(5\\theta)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )]^{8}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )]^{8}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=8$ and $\\phi =6\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )]^{8} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\cdot 6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot 6\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(48\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(48\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2392448160f40f4b2950be85e254ffe26679a0f9efd98c33f481c3aa954de7e"} {"question" "q-325338" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325338" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(48\\theta)-i\\sin(48\\theta)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-71459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expressi