.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2392448160f40f4b2950be85e254ffe26679a0f9efd98c33f481c3aa954de7e"} {"question" "q-325334" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325334" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(6\\theta)-i\\sin(6\\theta)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{6}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{6}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{6}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-6$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-6}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\theta )\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2392448160f40f4b2950be85e254ffe26679a0f9efd98c33f481c3aa954de7e"} {"question" "q-325344" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "q-325344" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(6\\theta)+i\\sin(6\\theta)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0b664fdfc17c5a0fb0cc22c02ac3b466d1e7a3a6eb1dd000f6857931357ba7d"} {"question" "e-5271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\left[ \\cos \\left( \\dfrac{\\theta}{10} \\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left( \\dfrac{\\theta}{10}\\right) \\right]^4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/example-5271.json" "file_sha256" "e395c7ccee2498257de1efd863464d180e9e02cdf014b9ed6d3ea2788257681d"} {"question" "e-5271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos(\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}.\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=4$ and $\\varphi=\\dfrac{\\theta}{10}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{10})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{10})]}^{4} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{10})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{10}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/example-5271.json" "file_sha256" "e395c7ccee2498257de1efd863464d180e9e02cdf014b9ed6d3ea2788257681d"} {"question" "e-5270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos (\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/example-5270.json" "file_sha256" "e9ac1a6863e153b1764890e89964ea536d9463ff7a1569e5eb70b7f52f6909ed"} {"question" "e-5270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos(\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^2} = \\left[ \\cos(\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^{-2} .\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos(\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}.\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-2$ and $\\varphi=\\theta.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{2}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\cos(-\\varphi) = \\cos (\\varphi)$ and $\\sin(-\\varphi) = -\\sin(\\varphi)$ for any input $\\varphi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos(-2\\theta) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(-2\\theta) = \\cos(2\\theta) - \\textrm{i}\\sin{(2\\theta)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/example-5270.json" "file_sha256" "e9ac1a6863e153b1764890e89964ea536d9463ff7a1569e5eb70b7f52f6909ed"} {"question" "e-5291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos (2\\theta) -\\textrm{i}\\sin (2\\theta) \\right]^4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/example-5291.json" "file_sha256" "3ac4e1f1bc9d1065813513df6b07a2effb00368f0577aeb366ef91bc26d9f0ee"} {"question" "e-5291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}^{4}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos (\\varphi) - \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) - \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}.\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\varphi=2\\theta.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}^{-4} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\cdot 2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\cdot 2\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\cos(-\\varphi) = \\cos (\\varphi)$ and $\\sin(-\\varphi) = -\\sin(\\varphi)$ for any input $\\varphi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055661/example-5291.json" "file_sha256" "3ac4e1f1bc9d1065813513df6b07a2effb00368f0577aeb366ef91bc26d9f0ee"}] "usage" {"e-5271" [] "e-5291" [] "e-5270" []} "basis" 1826 "retractions" [[17592186091981 :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\left[\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{10} \\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{10}\\right) \\right]^4$."] [17592186091981 :question/worked-solution "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos(\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=4$ and\n\n$$\n\\varphi=\\dfrac{\\theta}{10}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[\\cos (\\frac{θ}{10}) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (\\frac{θ}{10})]^{4} &= \\cos (4 \\cdot \\frac{θ}{10}) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (4 \\cdot \\frac{θ}{10}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{2θ}{5}) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (\\frac{2θ}{5})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186091980 :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{1}{\\left[\\cos (\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^2}$."] [17592186091980 :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos(\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^2} = \\left[ \\cos(\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^{-2}\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos(\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-2$ and\n\n$$\n\\varphi=\\theta\n$$\n\nSubstituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1)/([\\cos (θ) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (θ)]^{2}) &= [\\cos (θ) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (θ)]^{-2} \\\\\n&= \\cos (-2θ) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (-2θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\cos(-\\varphi) = \\cos (\\varphi)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\sin(-\\varphi) = -\\sin(\\varphi)\n$$\n\nfor any input $\\varphi$, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos(-2\\theta) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(-2\\theta) = \\cos(2\\theta) - \\textrm{i}\\sin{(2\\theta)}\n$$"] [17592186091987 :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{1}{\\left[\\cos (2\\theta) -\\textrm{i}\\sin (2\\theta) \\right]^4}$."] [17592186091987 :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1)/([\\cos (2θ) - \\textrm{i}\\sin (2θ)]^{4}) &= [\\cos (2θ) - \\textrm{i}\\sin (2θ)]^{-4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos (\\varphi) - \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) - \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and\n\n$$\n\\varphi=2\\theta\n$$\n\nSubstituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[\\cos (2θ) - \\textrm{i}\\sin (2θ)]^{-4} &= \\cos (-4 \\cdot 2θ) - \\textrm{i}\\sin (-4 \\cdot 2θ) \\\\\n&= \\cos (-8θ) - \\textrm{i}\\sin (-8θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\cos(-\\varphi) = \\cos (\\varphi)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\sin(-\\varphi) = -\\sin(\\varphi)\n$$\n\nfor any input $\\varphi$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (-8θ) - \\textrm{i}\\sin (-8θ) &= \\cos (8θ) - [- \\textrm{i}\\sin (8θ)] \\\\\n&= \\cos (8θ) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (8θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
